{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Observe the month of the aviv.</b> From before its arrival, watch that it be fit for aviv — to offer in it the meal-offering of the omer; and if not, intercalate the year (cf. Sanhedrin 11)." "<b>From Egypt by night.</b> But did they not go out by day, as it says ״מִמָּחֳרַת הַפֶּסַח יָצְאוּ בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״ (Numbers 33) and so forth? Rather, because at night Pharaoh gave them permission to leave, as it says ״וַיִּקְרָא לְמֹשֶׁה וּלְאַהֲרֹן לַיְלָה״ (Exodus 12) and so forth."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {1 "The parenthetical citation (בראשית ט') at the end of comment 1 is textually anomalous — it does not correspond to any verse relevant here and may be a copyist's error; translated as written."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:17.920594867Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}